IMPORT prelude

-- Montana Code Annotated 2025, Title 53, chapter 4, parts 2 and 6 (cash assistance funded by the federal TANF block
-- grant) -- the seat-neutral core: who is a dependent child (53-4-201(5)), who may be granted assistance and who is not
-- eligible (53-4-231), the application and the department's determination (53-4-232, 53-4-233), the amount (53-4-241:
-- by department rule, an input), the child support pass-through and disregard (53-4-260), child-care assistance
-- (53-4-611) and the employment and training condition (53-4-613).
--
-- Edition: Montana Code Annotated 2025 (laws through the 2025 session), site marked "Updated August 2026", as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/mca-53-4-part-2.txt and mca-53-4-part-6.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19 UTC).
-- The payment standards, income and resource tests are set by department rule (53-4-241; ARM Title 37, not deposited:
-- the rules.mt.gov terms could not be read, see subjects/us/mt/README.md), so the grant amount is an input.
--
-- The federal frame is 42 U.S.C. 601-619 (subjects/us/social-security-act/, usc42-ch7-schIV-ptA.txt): no individual
-- entitlement (s 601(b)), the 60-month limit (s 608(a)(7)), the fugitive felon and residence-fraud bars (s 608(a)(9),
-- s 408(a)(8)). Cross-folder IMPORT is not possible; NOTES.md names the link.
--
-- The seat questions are in mt-tanf-seat.l4. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Montana TANF cash assistance -- core`

§§ `53-4-201(5) -- dependent child`

-- "(a) (i) a child under 18 years of age; or (ii) a person under 19 years of age who is a student, as defined by the
-- department by rule. (b) ... must be living with a specified caretaker relative, as defined by the department by rule."
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
      `a student as the department's rule defines` IS A BOOLEAN
      `living with a specified caretaker relative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a dependent child` age `a student as the department's rule defines` `living with a specified caretaker relative` IF
        (    age LESS THAN 18
         OR  (age LESS THAN 19 AND `a student as the department's rule defines`))
    AND `living with a specified caretaker relative`

§§ `53-4-231 -- eligibility`

-- (1): assistance "may be granted" to (a) a dependent child; (b) a specified caretaker relative who (i) enters into an
-- individual responsibility plan if required and (ii) cooperates in required assessments and screening; (c) a
-- stepparent living with the child and the child's parent; (d) persons under 18 living in the home with a dependent
-- child; (e) a needy pregnant woman with no other children, from the third month before the expected birth.
-- (4): not eligible: (a) SSI recipients; (b) absence beyond the department's period; (c) failing to report a child's
-- absence; (d) the family, if the caretaker fails or refuses to assign child support rights or cooperate on paternity
-- or support; (e) the family, if the caretaker or another adult fails or refuses to cooperate in screening or
-- assessment, or to enter into an individual responsibility plan; (f) teenage parents not attending school or
-- training as required; (g) teenage parents not in an adult-supervised setting; (h) fugitive felons and probation or
-- parole violators; (i) for 10 years from conviction, fraudulent misrepresentation of residence.
-- (5): a family including an adult who has received TANF-funded cash assistance in any state for 60 months or more.
-- (2): non-citizens only as PRWORA ss 401-435 allow (an input). (3): a drug felony bars nothing while the person
-- complies with supervision or has discharged the sentence.
DECLARE `Household facts` HAS
    `the family includes a dependent child, or I am a needy pregnant woman with no other children` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months to the expected birth, if pregnant with no other children`                    IS A NUMBER
    `the caretaker entered an individual responsibility plan if required`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the caretaker and other adults cooperate in required screening and assessment`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the caretaker assigned support rights and cooperates on paternity and child support` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of TANF-funded cash assistance any adult in the family has received, in any state` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Person facts` HAS
    `receives SSI`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `a non-citizen not eligible under PRWORA ss 401 to 435`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `a fugitive felon or probation or parole violator`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of fraudulently misrepresenting residence within the last 10 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a drug felony and not complying with supervision or not discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a teenage parent not attending school or training as required, or not in an adult-supervised setting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `absent from the caretaker's home beyond the department's period`  IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Eligibility answer` IS ONE OF
    `assistance may be granted (there is no entitlement: 53-4-231(6))`
    `the family is not eligible: no dependent child in the home, and not a needy pregnant woman within 3 months of the birth`
    `the family is not eligible: an adult has received 60 months of TANF-funded cash assistance (53-4-231(5))`
    `the family is not eligible: support rights not assigned, or no cooperation on paternity or child support (53-4-231(4)(d))`
    `the family is not eligible: no cooperation in screening or assessment, or no individual responsibility plan (53-4-231(1)(b), (4)(e))`
    `this person is not eligible (53-4-231(2), (3) or (4))`

GIVEN h IS A `Household facts`, p IS A `Person facts`
GIVETH AN `Eligibility answer`
`the eligibility under 53-4-231` h p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT h's `the family includes a dependent child, or I am a needy pregnant woman with no other children`)
            THEN `the family is not eligible: no dependent child in the home, and not a needy pregnant woman within 3 months of the birth`
        IF h's `months to the expected birth, if pregnant with no other children` GREATER THAN 3
            THEN `the family is not eligible: no dependent child in the home, and not a needy pregnant woman within 3 months of the birth`
        IF h's `months of TANF-funded cash assistance any adult in the family has received, in any state` AT LEAST 60
            THEN `the family is not eligible: an adult has received 60 months of TANF-funded cash assistance (53-4-231(5))`
        IF (NOT h's `the caretaker assigned support rights and cooperates on paternity and child support`)
            THEN `the family is not eligible: support rights not assigned, or no cooperation on paternity or child support (53-4-231(4)(d))`
        IF     (NOT h's `the caretaker entered an individual responsibility plan if required`)
            OR (NOT h's `the caretaker and other adults cooperate in required screening and assessment`)
            THEN `the family is not eligible: no cooperation in screening or assessment, or no individual responsibility plan (53-4-231(1)(b), (4)(e))`
        IF     p's `receives SSI`
            OR p's `a non-citizen not eligible under PRWORA ss 401 to 435`
            OR p's `a fugitive felon or probation or parole violator`
            OR p's `convicted of fraudulently misrepresenting residence within the last 10 years`
            OR p's `a drug felony and not complying with supervision or not discharged`
            OR p's `a teenage parent not attending school or training as required, or not in an adult-supervised setting`
            OR p's `absent from the caretaker's home beyond the department's period`
            THEN `this person is not eligible (53-4-231(2), (3) or (4))`
        OTHERWISE `assistance may be granted (there is no entitlement: 53-4-231(6))`

§§ `53-4-260 -- child support pass-through and disregard`

-- (1): for families receiving monthly TANF grants, "an amount equal to the amount of current child support collected
-- on behalf of the family for the current month, not including arrearages, up to $100 for each family, must be
-- disregarded in determining the income and eligibility calculations for the grant, and that amount must be passed
-- through to the family".
GIVEN `current support collected this month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the support passed through and disregarded` `current support collected this month` MEANS
    min 100 (max 0 `current support collected this month`)

§§ `53-4-611, 53-4-613 -- child care, and employment and training`

-- 53-4-611: "Within available funding, the department may provide child-care assistance to: (1) all families receiving
-- cash assistance if child care is necessary to allow the parent to engage in paid employment; and (2) ... to engage in
-- the activities required by an individual responsibility plan." A discretion, so the answer is "may".
GIVEN `receiving cash assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `child care is needed for paid work or for my individual responsibility plan activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may get child-care assistance` `receiving cash assistance` `child care is needed for paid work or for my individual responsibility plan activities` IF
        `receiving cash assistance`
    AND `child care is needed for paid work or for my individual responsibility plan activities`

§§ `Duties: applying, the decision, screening, training`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `the department of public health and human services`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the department, as the relative the child lives or will live with`
    `make an eligibility determination and notify the applicant in writing`
    `inform the applicant of the right to a fair hearing and of confidentiality`
    `participate in the required screening`
    `furnish aid promptly`
    `participate in employment and training`

-- 53-4-232: "Application ... must be made to the department ... by the relative with whom the child is living or will
-- live. ... All individuals wishing to make application for this assistance must be given the opportunity to do so."
-- 53-4-233(1): "Upon receiving an application ... the department shall promptly make an eligibility determination and
-- notify the applicant in writing"; (2) "Each applicant shall participate in any screening required by the department
-- and must be informed of the applicant's right to a fair hearing and of the confidential nature of information"; (3)
-- "aid must be furnished promptly to all eligible persons". "Promptly" is not a number of days, so the rules carry no
-- WITHIN (NOTES.md finding 3).
GIVEN `found eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`what follows my application` `found eligible` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST  `apply to the department, as the relative the child lives or will live with`
    HENCE
        (PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST  `participate in the required screening`)
        RAND
        (PARTY `the department of public health and human services`
         MUST  `inform the applicant of the right to a fair hearing and of confidentiality`)
        RAND
        (PARTY `the department of public health and human services`
         MUST  `make an eligibility determination and notify the applicant in writing`
         HENCE
            (IF `found eligible`
             THEN PARTY `the department of public health and human services`
                  MUST  `furnish aid promptly`
             ELSE FULFILLED))

-- 53-4-613: where the department determines participation would be appropriate, "the recipient may be required to
-- participate in employment and training as one of the eligibility conditions".
-- The text gives no time; the days the department allows are an input.
GIVEN `the department requires me to participate` IS A BOOLEAN, `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the employment and training condition` `the department requires me to participate` `days allowed` MEANS
    IF `the department requires me to participate`
    THEN PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST  `participate in employment and training`
         WITHIN `days allowed`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "a recipient required to take part in employment and training did not, and it is one of the eligibility conditions (53-4-613)"
    ELSE FULFILLED
